and a fox news alert out of michigan at  this  hour as articles of impeachment are  introduced against governor gretchen  whitmer there  over the state's plan to enforce more  virus-related restrictions  brand new hour here in america's  newsroom welcome i'm sandra smith hi  trace  sandra good morning to you again good  morning everyone i'm trace gallagher  three michigan house republicans filing  the resolution  arguing governor whitmer's new limits on  gatherings violate the constitutional  rights of michigan citizens among other  things  the articles also accuse her of  corruption the governor's office has  dismissed the impeachment effort saying  quote  governor whitmer doesn't have any time  for partisan politics or people who  don't wear masks  don't believe in science and don't have  a plan to fight this  virus mike tobin live in chicago on this  developing story hey mike  and sandra it's important to note right  off the top although there's a great  deal of opposition to governor gretchen  whitmer  and her handling of the pandemic this  resolution does not have universal  support from michigan republicans in  fact  the leadership in both the state house  and the senate do not support it  lee chatfield the republican speaker of  the house told our fox affiliate  the resolution is a distraction from  what needs to be done in the state mike  shirkey the senate majority leader  says he has not signed on to the  resolution however three republicans in  the house representatives beau le fave  der rendon and matt murdock  introduced the resolution arguing that  governor whitmer should be removed from  office for corrupt conduct crimes and  misdemeanors  part of the resolution reads she has  exceeded her constitutional authority  violated the constitutional rights of  the people of michigan issued orders  that are not in the best interests of  the people of the state and use the  pandemic as an opportunity  to reward political allies the  resolution argues that whitmer bypassed  the legislature with executive orders  ban free exercise of religion  offered no-bid contracts to political  allies and failed to manage the crisis  now whitmer has come under fire for the  harsh and critics say arbitrary nature  of the lockdowns in michigan  the wolverine state just extended the  shutdown for three weeks  whitmer used the word pause one of the  authors of the resolution matt murdock  reportedly said that  was the tipping point it should be noted  that michigan has seen a 29  increase in coronavirus cases over the  past week  sandra mike tobin thank you
 

